{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Managing the Restaurant", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Customer Loyalty ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 4, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe emotions and feelings in present and past situations in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands extended speeches, lectures, articles and reports of the professional, academic, or daily life on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Integrates factual information to a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Consonant Clusters: th and nt", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Consonant clusters are groups of two consonants or more together. They form a specific sound when they are combined in a particular way. Usually the sounds of some of the consonants may be reduced or dropped. <br/><br/> In -th consonant clusters, the /th/ sound can be changed or dropped to sound more like a /t/ sound. In the plural form of words ending in th, the final sound can be /s/ or /z/. <br/><span class=\"strong\">Example</span>: <span class=\"italic\">months = /mons/</span><br/><br/>In -nt consonant clusters, the /t/ sound can be dropped if it is followed by a vowel sound. In that case, a flapped /n/ is used in its place.<span class=\"strong\"><br/>Examples</span>: <span class=\"italic\">center = /cen'ner/ or </span><span class=\"italic\">twenty = /twen'ny/</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Practice reading the following sentences aloud:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Layered programs are sometimes added to a core loyalty program to add <span class =\"strong\">depth</span> and tailor it to a specific type of guest.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You want to develop a program that will grab your guests' attention and encourage <span class=\"strong\">incremental </span>increases in spending over time.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Your promotions should <span class=\"strong\">accentuate</span> that signature item on your menu. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Intonation in Lists", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you talk about lists, it is important to use the right stress and intonation. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When naming items in a list, you use rising intonation for the first item in the list and falling intonation for the last. Falling intonation indicates the end of the list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Example:</span> <span class=\"italic\">It explains the program's rewards and how they are \u2197<span class=\"strong\">earned</span>, \u2197<span class=\"strong\">redeemed</span>, and \u2198<span class=\"strong\">how they expire</span>. </span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Practice the following sentences from the text:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Every loyalty program is comprised of three basic elements: <span class=\"strong\">a core program</span>, <span class=\"strong\">layered programs</span> and <span class=\"strong\">promotions</span>.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It highlights the distinctive character of your restaurant in a way that  <span class=\"strong\">appeals to guests</span>, <span class=\"strong\">encourages them to visit frequently</span> and <span class=\"strong\">gets them spending more money when they visit<span class=\"strong\">.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "An effective promotion will <span class=\"strong\">generate traffic in the slow periods of the day</span>, <span class=\"strong\">inspire customers to try new menu items</span>, <span class=\"strong\">and keep the restaurant in the minds of customers</span>.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "distinctive ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "being different or having a unique quality or characteristic", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It highlights the distinctive character of your restaurant.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about loyalty programs. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "underlying ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "important not easily noticed ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The underlying structure of a loyalty program is the core program. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to redeem ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to exchange something for goods equal to its value  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Rewards programs need to explain clearly how points can be redeemed. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "incremental ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "increasing in amount gradually ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You want to develop a program that will grab your guests' attention and encourage incremental increases in spending over time. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to accentuate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make something more noticeable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Your promotions should accentuate that signature item on your menu. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "complementary", "type": "name"}, {"content": "go well together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Encourage customers to come for that specific dish, and also to try complementary products.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "lever", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something you use to influence a situation to get the result that you want", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They give you a lever to engage with your guests, discover their preferences and encourage more frequent visits.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to generate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to produce or cause something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  An effective promotion will generate more traffic in the slow periods of the day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn11le05ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": " Research 3 stores in your city. These could be supermarkets or other retail stores.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go online or to the stores themselves.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Answer the following questions about these stores: What loyalty programs do they have for customers? Do they offer a special card for loyal customers? What are the advantages and disadvantages of joining the programs? Do you or your friends belong to any programs? Would you ever sign up for one?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Discuss your findings in groups. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I identify the loyalty programs in 3 stores in my city.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I give my opinion about different loyalty programs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I discuss loyalty programs in a group.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about work and dealing with customers.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say and use words like month and accentuate. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can use proper intonati