g in your restaurant. Every loyalty program is comprised of three basic elements: a core program, layered programs and promotions.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn11le05ob04re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "The core program is the heart of any restaurant loyalty program. Its purpose is to attract guests to join other loyal customers and frequent your restaurant. It highlights the distinctive character of your restaurant in a way that appeals to guests, encourages them to visit and gets them spending more money when they visit. The underlying structure of a loyalty program is the core program. It explains the program's rewards and how they are earned, redeemed, and how they expire.", "id": 2, "time": "13500", "image": "engenn11le05ob04re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "You want to develop a program that will grab your guests' attention and encourage incremental increases in spending over time. The core loyalty program selected by your restaurant should enable promotions and showcase it or its type of cuisine. For example, if a signature item anchors your menu, your promotions should accentuate that signature item on the menu to encourage customers to come for that specific dish, and also to try complementary products. On the other hand, an eclectic, dynamic menu lends itself to promotions that encourage guests to try lots of different items, and to come for lunch as well as dinner.", "id": 3, "time": "40500", "image": "engenn11le05ob04re2img02.jpg"}, {"text": "Layered programs are sometimes added to a core loyalty program to add depth and tailor it to a specific type of guest, and to strengthen your guests' connection to the restaurant. For example, a birthday promotion of a free meal or dessert could entice people to celebrate their special day at your restaurant.", "id": 4, "time": "75000", "image": "engenn11le05ob04re2img03.jpg"}, {"text": "You can influence your guests' buying behavior by using promotion programs. They give you a lever that enables you to engage with your guests, discover their preferences and encourage more frequent visits. An effective promotion will generate more traffic in the slow periods of the day, inspire customers to try new menu items, and keep the restaurant in the minds of customers.", "id": 5, "time": "92500", "image": "engenn11le05ob04re2img03.jpg"}], "audiosrc": "engenn11le05ob04re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn11le05ob04re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "_data": [], "type": "audio", "template_override": 1}]}]}